WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:00:03.080 --> 00:00:08.150
Gold Roger, the legendary King of the Pirates, obtained everything the world has to offer.

3
00:00:08.150 --> 00:00:12.890
What he said in his final moments drove countless souls to the seas.

4
00:00:12.890 --> 00:00:17.430
You want my treasure? Go ahead. Find it!

5
00:00:17.430 --> 00:00:19.830
Everything is right where I left it!

6
00:00:19.830 --> 00:00:22.840
Pirates have set out in pursuit of their dreams!

7
00:00:22.840 --> 00:00:25.440
The world has truly entered... the Great Pirate Era!

8
00:00:25.310 --> 00:00:29.380
Gotta keep movin’, just can't stop

9
00:00:29.380 --> 00:00:33.780
Rarin’ for the dawn to arrive

10
00:00:33.780 --> 00:00:37.480
One, two, sunshine, four, we go!

11
00:00:38.920 --> 00:00:43.290
Hoist the flag for the break of romance dawn

12
00:00:44.390 --> 00:00:49.500
Jump-start your day, ready to make waves

13
00:00:49.730 --> 00:00:54.200
Reachin’ for fantastic realms

14
00:00:54.330 --> 00:00:58.370
Need to put your toughness on display

15
00:00:58.940 --> 00:01:01.680
Is bein’ brazen such a crime?

16
00:01:01.780 --> 00:01:04.480
If you’re wanted, you’re a winner

17
00:01:04.710 --> 00:01:09.620
Ah, freedom is our only rule

18
00:01:10.380 --> 00:01:15.660
Worries don’t bother us at all

19
00:01:15.820 --> 00:01:18.430
Keep on goin’, that's our pledge

20
00:01:18.430 --> 00:01:22.030
Since the day our dreams began

21
00:01:22.460 --> 00:01:26.870
Our aims remain the same

22
00:01:26.870 --> 00:01:29.240
Sunlight won’t fade from our hearts

23
00:01:29.300 --> 00:01:33.670
The sun of my heart will never set

24
00:01:33.710 --> 00:01:40.450
One, two, sunshine... One, two, sunshine

25
00:01:41.750 --> 00:01:47.850
One, two, sunshine, four, we go!

26
00:01:50.160 --> 00:01:51.930
We go!

27
00:01:53.300 --> 00:01:58.640
<b>Island of New Beginnings</b>

28
00:01:58.990 --> 00:02:00.690
Come on.

29
00:02:00.690 --> 00:02:02.930
Just apologize already!

30
00:02:02.930 --> 00:02:05.830
Don't you have
something you wanna live for?

31
00:02:05.830 --> 00:02:06.680
Heh.

32
00:02:06.680 --> 00:02:08.700
Well, kid? What'cha thinkin'?

33
00:02:09.700 --> 00:02:12.270
You screwed up and
now it's time to pay!

34
00:02:12.270 --> 00:02:13.840
So, speak up.

35
00:02:14.840 --> 00:02:16.610
Please! Take a look at that brat.

36
00:02:16.610 --> 00:02:18.780
Obviously you scared
him silent, Captain!

37
00:02:19.610 --> 00:02:21.340
I can't blame the kid.

38
00:02:21.340 --> 00:02:22.840
After that guy with the schnoz

39
00:02:22.840 --> 00:02:25.040
and that chick with the long
hair picked a fight with us,

40
00:02:25.040 --> 00:02:27.350
we're in a worse mood than usual.

41
00:02:27.350 --> 00:02:32.320
Now, if you don't wanna be our personal
punching bag, you'd best ask forgiveness.

42
00:02:32.320 --> 00:02:34.330
Kneel! Get down in the dirt!

43
00:02:34.330 --> 00:02:35.670
Forget your pride.

44
00:02:35.670 --> 00:02:39.660
Otherwise, you're gonna end up throwin'
your life away over some small mistake.

45
00:02:39.660 --> 00:02:43.030
After all, our captain's trigger
finger can be a little twitchy.

46
00:02:46.450 --> 00:02:47.950
C'mon, kid, just do it!

47
00:02:47.950 --> 00:02:50.720
You shouldn't mess around
with Straw Hat Luffy!

48
00:02:50.720 --> 00:02:53.400
You're gonna die if
you don't do what he says!

49
00:02:53.400 --> 00:02:55.570
All right, look. I'm sorry.

50
00:02:55.570 --> 00:02:57.540
Now I got somewhere to be.

51
00:02:58.980 --> 00:03:01.880
– What's wrong with you?
– What's wrong with you?

52
00:03:06.880 --> 00:03:11.420
Bad move. Say goodbye, punk!

53
00:03:45.090 --> 00:03:46.660
What happened?

54
00:03:50.190 --> 00:03:53.580
Hey. That guy... Did he do somethin'?

55
00:03:59.150 --> 00:04:01.320
Why you bein' such an ass about this?

56
00:04:01.320 --> 00:04:02.450
I just wanna go fish.

57
00:04:02.450 --> 00:04:04.050
Well, too bad, you can't!

58
00:04:04.050 --> 00:04:05.590
Give me one good reason!

59
00:04:05.590 --> 00:04:09.160
And while you're at it, give me one good
reason why I should even listen to you!

60
00:04:09.160 --> 00:04:13.310
I don't wanna hang out together any more
than you do, but I can't let you get lost!

61
00:04:13.310 --> 00:04:14.670
Don't get me wrong, though.

62
00:04:14.670 --> 00:04:17.570
Nothing would make me happier
than leaving you here for good.

63
00:04:17.570 --> 00:04:18.800
Too bad, huh?

64
00:04:18.800 --> 00:04:20.870
The point is, everyone's
meeting on the ship,

65
00:04:20.870 --> 00:04:23.490
so you don't get to go
fishing on your own!

66
00:04:23.490 --> 00:04:24.890
Tch.

67
00:04:26.430 --> 00:04:28.100
What a joke.

68
00:04:29.390 --> 00:04:33.260
Number seven thinks he can talk crap
to number one and get away with it.

69
00:04:33.260 --> 00:04:36.170
You think you're better than me
just 'cause you got here first?

70
00:04:36.170 --> 00:04:38.840
It's not like everyone swam
to Sabaody, all right?

71
00:04:38.840 --> 00:04:41.010
You got nothin' to brag about!

72
00:04:41.010 --> 00:04:45.180
Sure, whatever you say, number seven.

73
00:04:45.180 --> 00:04:47.810
Fine! You wanna fight me?

74
00:04:47.810 --> 00:04:51.420
I trained these legs on the
shores of hell for two years!

75
00:04:51.420 --> 00:04:53.150
Then you better use them to run.

76
00:04:53.150 --> 00:04:54.790
'Cause I will cut you in half!

77
00:05:00.220 --> 00:05:01.730
Captain Luffy!

78
00:05:01.730 --> 00:05:02.890
Aw, man, you okay?

79
00:05:04.110 --> 00:05:05.490
Ugh. Dammit!

80
00:05:05.860 --> 00:05:08.600
Luffy!

81
00:05:08.600 --> 00:05:11.700
Oh my gosh, I missed you guys so much!

82
00:05:11.700 --> 00:05:13.170
It's me!

83
00:05:13.170 --> 00:05:14.170
Hey, Luffy!

84
00:05:14.170 --> 00:05:15.470
Huh?

85
00:05:15.470 --> 00:05:16.600
Franky!

86
00:05:16.600 --> 00:05:17.540
Eh?

87
00:05:17.540 --> 00:05:18.470
Nami!

88
00:05:18.470 --> 00:05:19.340
Huh?

89
00:05:22.880 --> 00:05:25.450
Sniper King?

90
00:05:25.450 --> 00:05:27.780
Awesome!

91
00:05:27.780 --> 00:05:30.800
But, wow, you sure changed
a lot in two years, huh?

92
00:05:30.800 --> 00:05:33.440
I bet you're all super strong now!

93
00:05:34.670 --> 00:05:36.530
What're the Straw Hats up to?

94
00:05:36.530 --> 00:05:39.100
They're just sitting.
Did something happen?

95
00:05:39.100 --> 00:05:40.700
Uh, yeah, but keep it down.

96
00:05:40.700 --> 00:05:42.570
They're pissed off, so
don't look 'em in the eye.

97
00:05:42.570 --> 00:05:44.740
You don't wanna pick
a fight with these guys.

98
00:05:46.670 --> 00:05:48.460
Eh? What the hell?

99
00:05:48.460 --> 00:05:50.710
Whoa, what happened, boss?

100
00:05:51.410 --> 00:05:53.320
It was messed up!

101
00:05:53.320 --> 00:05:56.320
Like, all of a sudden,
I got these chills!

102
00:05:57.710 --> 00:05:59.770
Never seen a trick like that before!

103
00:06:00.820 --> 00:06:04.060
Oh, I forgot. We got another
problem, actually.

104
00:06:04.060 --> 00:06:09.110
The thing is, Cocoa...uh, I mean,
Robin is in a real pickle right now.

105
00:06:09.460 --> 00:06:10.960
She was kidnapped?!

106
00:06:10.960 --> 00:06:12.990
And you let the bastards go?

107
00:06:12.990 --> 00:06:16.500
Yeah, sorry. I mean,
it all happened so fast.

108
00:06:16.500 --> 00:06:19.330
They must be human traffickers!
This could be real bad!

109
00:06:19.330 --> 00:06:21.070
They could try to sell her at auction!

110
00:06:21.070 --> 00:06:23.140
Like what happened with Camie!

111
00:06:25.210 --> 00:06:26.500
Get a good look at them?

112
00:06:26.780 --> 00:06:29.680
No. Like I said,
it happened all sudden-like.

113
00:06:29.680 --> 00:06:34.450
Hey, Captain, they musta nabbed Cocoa
'cause they thought she was the real Robin.

114
00:06:34.450 --> 00:06:37.160
We might be in over our heads here.

115
00:06:37.160 --> 00:06:39.240
I shoulda known. You're right.

116
00:06:39.240 --> 00:06:41.540
She does look just like the real thing.

117
00:06:41.540 --> 00:06:44.980
Guess that worked against us this time.

118
00:06:44.980 --> 00:06:47.250
Hey! Are you keeping secrets from me?

119
00:06:47.250 --> 00:06:48.550
Huh?

120
00:06:49.990 --> 00:06:52.230
I don't care. Leave her!

121
00:06:52.230 --> 00:06:54.000
It's not our problem if she dies.

122
00:06:54.770 --> 00:06:55.730
What? Uh, okay.

123
00:06:56.820 --> 00:07:01.040
Are you nuts? Luffy,
Robin is our friend!

124
00:07:01.040 --> 00:07:05.530
Listen, what is this thing?
And why does it talk?

125
00:07:05.530 --> 00:07:08.130
If this is supposed to be
a joke, it's not funny!

126
00:07:08.130 --> 00:07:10.610
We lost Robin once...
don't kid about that!

127
00:07:10.610 --> 00:07:13.470
See, it's doing it again!
It can't be a toy.

128
00:07:13.470 --> 00:07:14.970
Take it back, Luffy!

129
00:07:14.970 --> 00:07:16.410
Get offa me!

130
00:07:20.260 --> 00:07:21.930
All right, screw the thing with Robin

131
00:07:21.930 --> 00:07:23.530
and screw this stuffed animal thing.

132
00:07:23.530 --> 00:07:28.550
We gotta get our whole team together
here on Grove 46, and pronto!

133
00:07:28.550 --> 00:07:30.610
That punk with the long nose.

134
00:07:30.610 --> 00:07:32.470
That woman with the orange hair.

135
00:07:32.780 --> 00:07:35.230
And that crappy kid
with the giant backpack.

136
00:07:36.340 --> 00:07:39.050
Hunt them down and kick their asses.

137
00:07:39.050 --> 00:07:43.740
We're gonna show the whole damn world what
happens when you cross Straw Hat Luffy!

138
00:07:43.740 --> 00:07:45.180
– Uh, roger!
– Uh, roger!

139
00:07:45.180 --> 00:07:48.900
Don't kill 'em yet, so we can make
a good show of it, huh, Captain?

140
00:07:48.900 --> 00:07:53.040
We'll drag 'em through the streets till
everyone on Sabaody's shaking in fear!

141
00:07:53.040 --> 00:07:54.410
Works for me!

142
00:07:54.410 --> 00:07:55.710
Are you crazy?!

143
00:07:55.710 --> 00:07:58.710
Cut it out! It's only been two years!

144
00:07:58.710 --> 00:08:01.650
What happened to you? This is wrong!

145
00:08:01.650 --> 00:08:03.480
I don't know. I'm just...

146
00:08:03.480 --> 00:08:05.270
I'm so sad right now.

147
00:08:05.270 --> 00:08:07.430
You're making me cry!

148
00:08:07.430 --> 00:08:10.550
For the last time,
what is this stupid thing?

149
00:08:10.550 --> 00:08:12.650
And none of you wanna help Robin?

150
00:08:12.650 --> 00:08:14.650
Nobody's gonna say anything?

151
00:08:14.650 --> 00:08:17.220
Why's this runt so
attached to us, anyway?

152
00:08:17.220 --> 00:08:19.790
When we're done here,
maybe we should try selling it.

153
00:08:19.790 --> 00:08:21.460
Damn it, forget this!

154
00:08:21.460 --> 00:08:23.630
I don't have time to argue with you!

155
00:08:23.630 --> 00:08:27.400
I'll save her on my own!
I don't need you!

156
00:08:31.330 --> 00:08:34.770
I'm coming, Robin! Hold on!

157
00:08:37.230 --> 00:08:38.370
What was that? They have a fight?

158
00:08:40.630 --> 00:08:41.510
I dunno. But it's definitely them.

159
00:08:43.840 --> 00:08:47.010
I mean, they haven't aged
well in the past two years,

160
00:08:47.010 --> 00:08:49.510
but nobody else has
a weird pet like that.

161
00:08:49.510 --> 00:08:52.950
Looks like the reports
are true after all.

162
00:08:52.950 --> 00:08:56.520
They're alive. The Straw Hats are back!

163
00:08:56.520 --> 00:08:59.200
And they're causing trouble again!

164
00:08:59.200 --> 00:09:01.300
This is Grove #47.

165
00:09:02.050 --> 00:09:05.890
It's them. We've sighted six
Straw Hats and their pet!

166
00:09:08.930 --> 00:09:12.670
<b>Naval Station, Grove 66</b>

167
00:09:09.920 --> 00:09:13.730
The rumors that they recruited other
pirates seem to be true as well.

168
00:09:13.730 --> 00:09:17.110
They should be assembling on
Grove #46 any minute now!

169
00:09:17.110 --> 00:09:19.950
Understood! Then we'd
better move quickly.

170
00:09:19.950 --> 00:09:22.450
Evacuate the locals before
this becomes a war zone!

171
00:09:22.450 --> 00:09:23.620
Roger!

172
00:09:23.620 --> 00:09:25.650
Pirates are gathering at Grove 46.

173
00:09:25.650 --> 00:09:27.660
Our targets are the Straw Hats.

174
00:09:27.660 --> 00:09:29.690
We'll engage them in the lawless zone.

175
00:09:29.690 --> 00:09:31.330
They may have reinforcements!

176
00:09:31.330 --> 00:09:32.960
Block all routes of escape!

177
00:09:32.960 --> 00:09:36.510
Close in on them from
Groves 40, 42, and 44!

178
00:09:36.510 --> 00:09:38.050
Make it snappy!

179
00:09:38.050 --> 00:09:40.680
G1 is sending in backup now!

180
00:09:47.350 --> 00:09:49.710
Sentomaru, sir!

181
00:09:50.140 --> 00:09:51.810
I'm heading in first.

182
00:09:52.350 --> 00:09:56.110
PX-5 and PX-7 will accompany me.

183
00:09:56.110 --> 00:09:59.620
Whoa. You're deploying Pacifistas, sir?

184
00:09:59.620 --> 00:10:01.320
Of course I am!

185
00:10:03.280 --> 00:10:04.480
You fools.

186
00:10:04.480 --> 00:10:08.000
Haven't you learned not to
underestimate the Straw Hats?

187
00:10:08.000 --> 00:10:10.370
It's been two years since the war.

188
00:10:10.370 --> 00:10:13.480
Surely they've only grown
stronger during that time.

189
00:10:13.480 --> 00:10:18.250
They may be rookies, but make no mistake,
they're the most dangerous pirates here.

190
00:10:19.980 --> 00:10:24.770
As for what happened last time,
we were never able to determine

191
00:10:24.770 --> 00:10:28.010
why Kuma sent them away instead
of apprehending them.

192
00:10:30.510 --> 00:10:34.850
But even after his personality was
wiped, his actions seemed to indicate

193
00:10:34.850 --> 00:10:37.180
that they would be
returning here someday.

194
00:10:37.180 --> 00:10:40.790
And now that they have, we must
ensure that this doesn't end

195
00:10:40.790 --> 00:10:42.590
like it did two years ago.

196
00:10:42.590 --> 00:10:44.150
Let's move!

197
00:10:58.980 --> 00:11:05.620
<b>Sabaody Archipelago
Grove 35</b>

198
00:11:06.260 --> 00:11:09.500
Damn it! Damn it! Damn it!

199
00:11:09.500 --> 00:11:11.100
Damn it!

200
00:11:12.500 --> 00:11:14.030
None of this makes sense!

201
00:11:14.030 --> 00:11:16.800
Why are they acting that way?

202
00:11:16.800 --> 00:11:22.480
Luffy, Zoro, Nami, Sanji, Franky.

203
00:11:22.480 --> 00:11:25.350
What happened to them? Why?

204
00:11:26.400 --> 00:11:29.640
Robin gets taken away,
and you don't care?

205
00:11:31.810 --> 00:11:34.160
What's wrong with you?

206
00:11:34.160 --> 00:11:39.290
I've been working so hard these past
two years to be a better doctor.

207
00:11:39.290 --> 00:11:40.890
But for what?

208
00:11:44.580 --> 00:11:46.490
Chopper!

209
00:11:46.490 --> 00:11:47.860
Hey!

210
00:11:51.040 --> 00:11:52.230
Yoo-hoo! Over here!

211
00:11:53.770 --> 00:11:57.240
I could tell it was you
from a mile away!

212
00:11:57.240 --> 00:11:59.280
Ah!

213
00:11:59.280 --> 00:12:00.680
It's Usopp!

214
00:12:00.960 --> 00:12:04.100
Jeez, you got so big! Just look at you!

215
00:12:04.100 --> 00:12:06.940
I bet I could even ride
on your back, couldn't I?

216
00:12:06.940 --> 00:12:08.280
You doin' okay?

217
00:12:08.280 --> 00:12:09.150
Uh-huh!

218
00:12:09.700 --> 00:12:14.440
So cuddly! I'm sure the lady
reindeers just adore you!

219
00:12:14.440 --> 00:12:17.630
I missed you, Chopper. So much!

220
00:12:17.630 --> 00:12:19.470
Uhh...

221
00:12:20.990 --> 00:12:22.070
Uh, Nami?

222
00:12:22.070 --> 00:12:22.930
Uh-huh?

223
00:12:24.590 --> 00:12:25.700
Wait a second!

224
00:12:26.010 --> 00:12:29.810
I'm happy to see you guys and all,
but now's not the time for this.

225
00:12:29.810 --> 00:12:32.050
Robin is in serious trouble!

226
00:12:37.310 --> 00:12:39.940
Huh? They're just pretending to be you?

227
00:12:40.570 --> 00:12:42.100
That's why there's two Namis?

228
00:12:43.440 --> 00:12:45.140
Use your head, okay?

229
00:12:45.140 --> 00:12:48.740
Robin was able to avoid
the government for 20 years.

230
00:12:48.740 --> 00:12:52.090
Do you really think someone could
just grab her and stuff her in a bag?

231
00:12:52.090 --> 00:12:53.690
No offense, but come on!

232
00:12:53.690 --> 00:12:54.660
I see!

233
00:12:54.660 --> 00:12:59.260
I have a tough time telling humans apart,
but she didn't even smell right.

234
00:13:01.530 --> 00:13:03.770
Darn it, now I'm starting to get mad!

235
00:13:03.770 --> 00:13:07.810
If we see one of them again, I'm gonna
punch 'em in their big, fake face!

236
00:13:07.810 --> 00:13:10.680
They've got some nerve,
pretending to be us!

237
00:13:10.680 --> 00:13:13.370
I mean, why would they do
that in the first place?

238
00:13:15.130 --> 00:13:17.670
It's almost like we're
celebrities or something.

239
00:13:17.670 --> 00:13:19.370
That's crazy!

240
00:13:19.370 --> 00:13:21.710
Hey, don't let it go to your head.

241
00:13:21.710 --> 00:13:25.670
Although you aren't that far off, since
our captain worked up quite a reputation

242
00:13:25.670 --> 00:13:27.240
for fighting in that war.

243
00:13:28.270 --> 00:13:30.120
Hah. I have to
come up with a cool autograph.

244
00:13:30.120 --> 00:13:32.460
Heh. I've already got one!

245
00:13:32.460 --> 00:13:36.770
Come on, you two, we're famous
criminals, not celebrities.

246
00:13:42.070 --> 00:13:45.020
Chopper! Where'd you go?

247
00:13:45.920 --> 00:13:47.990
Come back!

248
00:13:47.990 --> 00:13:48.910
Ugh. This sucks!

249
00:13:48.910 --> 00:13:50.980
That little dude was
their pet for real!

250
00:13:50.980 --> 00:13:53.480
He, like, doubled our credibility!

251
00:13:54.650 --> 00:13:56.490
Ow, my side hurts.

252
00:13:56.490 --> 00:13:58.050
Are you nuts?

253
00:13:58.050 --> 00:14:00.160
That talking stuffed
animal thing was part

254
00:14:00.160 --> 00:14:02.990
of the real Straw Hats
and you let it get away?

255
00:14:02.990 --> 00:14:04.830
Why didn't you tell me?

256
00:14:04.830 --> 00:14:06.820
And why aren't you looking for it?

257
00:14:08.660 --> 00:14:10.070
Oh, sure, go look for him.

258
00:14:10.070 --> 00:14:11.970
Like we have any idea where he went!

259
00:14:11.970 --> 00:14:15.530
Yeah, I mean, Sabaody is super
big and that guy was teeny tiny.

260
00:14:15.530 --> 00:14:18.670
I can't do this. I am dyin' here!

261
00:14:21.550 --> 00:14:25.390
Forget runnin'. We'll walk. Power walk.

262
00:14:26.410 --> 00:14:27.640
Hancock was right.

263
00:14:27.640 --> 00:14:30.750
With all the pirates around,
this mustache is pretty handy.

264
00:14:30.750 --> 00:14:33.280
I don't wanna fight with
those guys anyway.

265
00:14:35.970 --> 00:14:37.870
Look! It's that kid with the backpack!

266
00:14:37.870 --> 00:14:40.540
Maybe our luck ain't so bad after all!

267
00:14:40.540 --> 00:14:41.710
Boss called him a "kid,"

268
00:14:41.710 --> 00:14:45.250
but he kinda looks like
an old man to me.

269
00:14:45.250 --> 00:14:47.550
Oh, it's you guys.

270
00:14:49.690 --> 00:14:52.490
Hey, friend. We need
you to come with us.

271
00:14:52.490 --> 00:14:54.560
Let's do this nice and quiet, okay?

272
00:14:54.560 --> 00:14:56.000
We don't want any trouble.

273
00:14:56.000 --> 00:14:58.470
You really pissed
off our captain, kiddo.

274
00:14:58.470 --> 00:15:01.700
I'd prepare for the worst if I was you.

275
00:15:01.700 --> 00:15:04.310
What's wrong? You so scared
you can't even talk?

276
00:15:04.310 --> 00:15:06.570
Hey, Sanji. How's it goin'?

277
00:15:07.510 --> 00:15:09.210
And Zoro, too. Wow!

278
00:15:09.210 --> 00:15:11.280
Long time no see, huh, guys?

279
00:15:11.280 --> 00:15:14.250
Oh. Uh-huh! Too long, right?

280
00:15:15.620 --> 00:15:17.880
Yeah, well, let's get goin' then. Heh.

281
00:15:17.880 --> 00:15:20.050
You mean the rest of
the crew's here already?

282
00:15:20.050 --> 00:15:23.580
Sorry I was so late!
Good thing you found me!

283
00:15:27.810 --> 00:15:31.210
Well, he knows the Straw Hats,
but we don't know him.

284
00:15:31.210 --> 00:15:32.900
Like I care!

285
00:15:32.900 --> 00:15:35.120
Just take him to Luffy
and he'll sort this out!

286
00:15:39.690 --> 00:15:45.130
<b>Straw Hat Rendezvous Point, Grove 46</b>

287
00:15:49.470 --> 00:15:51.630
Reporting from Grove 46.

288
00:15:52.740 --> 00:15:54.210
All the new recruits the Straw Hats

289
00:15:54.210 --> 00:15:56.350
picked up are gathering here,
and from the looks of things,

290
00:15:56.350 --> 00:15:58.650
I'd say there might be
nearly a hundred of them.

291
00:15:58.650 --> 00:16:02.150
Most of them are nobodies,
but there are four captains at least.

292
00:16:01.510 --> 00:16:06.050
<b>Albion "the Maimed"
Bounty: 92 Million</b>

293
00:16:02.150 --> 00:16:06.090
I see "Gashed" Albion for one.
He's worth 92 million.

294
00:16:06.080 --> 00:16:10.790
<b>Lip "Service" Doughty
Bounty: 88 Million</b>

295
00:16:06.090 --> 00:16:10.530
Then there's "Lip-Service" Doughty,
who's worth 88 million.

296
00:16:12.090 --> 00:16:15.430
But those aren't the ones
I'm really worried about.

297
00:16:15.330 --> 00:16:22.570
<b>"Wet-Haired" Caribou
Bounty: 210 Million</b>

298
00:16:15.430 --> 00:16:19.430
They've also got "Wet-Haired"
Caribou, worth 210 million.

299
00:16:19.430 --> 00:16:22.700
The captain of his crew.

300
00:16:22.630 --> 00:16:30.210
<b>"Blood Spatter" Coribou
Bounty: 190 Million</b>

301
00:16:22.700 --> 00:16:26.270
He brought his brother with him,
"Blood Splatter" Coribou.

302
00:16:26.270 --> 00:16:29.080
His bounty's at 190 million.

303
00:16:37.850 --> 00:16:43.790
<b>Sabao Dome
Grove 33</b>

304
00:16:49.590 --> 00:16:52.650
The Navy is here? So they know.

305
00:16:53.500 --> 00:16:54.560
Very well, then.

306
00:16:54.560 --> 00:16:56.500
Take it easy! No pushing!

307
00:16:56.500 --> 00:16:58.740
One more song, Soul King!
We're waiting for you!

308
00:16:58.740 --> 00:17:01.490
I still need a moment more.

309
00:17:00.710 --> 00:17:04.550
My fans are calling for an encore,
you see, and I can't let them down.

310
00:17:10.060 --> 00:17:12.230
I think I owe them this much at least.

311
00:17:12.230 --> 00:17:14.490
So please, wait up for me.

312
00:17:31.000 --> 00:17:33.940
Those cheers could bring a dead
man back from his grave, baby.

313
00:17:39.580 --> 00:17:42.780
This is the Navy! Nobody move!

314
00:17:42.780 --> 00:17:44.980
What's the deal? That's not cool!

315
00:17:44.980 --> 00:17:49.080
This is last living member of the Rumbar
Pirates, the "Humming Swordsman" Brook,

316
00:17:49.080 --> 00:17:52.760
presumed dead until now,
with a bounty of 33 million.

317
00:17:52.760 --> 00:17:57.500
Despite his skeletal state, our reports
indicate that Soul King is this pirate.

318
00:17:57.500 --> 00:18:01.130
In addition to his previous crimes,
we have further information that indicates

319
00:18:01.130 --> 00:18:04.120
he is now working for Straw Hat Luffy!

320
00:18:04.120 --> 00:18:10.290
Soul King Brook, or rather, Humming Swordsman
Brook, you're under arrest for piracy!

321
00:18:13.570 --> 00:18:15.670
No, it can't be true!

322
00:18:15.670 --> 00:18:18.170
I feel like my whole life is a lie.

323
00:18:18.170 --> 00:18:19.740
He was a pirate all along?

324
00:18:19.740 --> 00:18:23.480
But wait, Straw Hat Luffy's
been missing for years now.

325
00:18:23.480 --> 00:18:26.670
It's been a good
run, Brook, but it's over.

326
00:18:26.670 --> 00:18:31.140
Your betrayal's not exactly
a surprise, Mr. Manager.

327
00:18:31.140 --> 00:18:35.180
You're the one to blame, telling me you
were gonna retire right after the show.

328
00:18:35.180 --> 00:18:37.110
How could you do this to me?

329
00:18:37.110 --> 00:18:39.520
A pity, but it seems like
I would've been better off

330
00:18:39.520 --> 00:18:42.390
keeping you in that cage after all.

331
00:18:42.390 --> 00:18:45.460
We were gonna be rich,
but now our company's ruined.

332
00:18:45.460 --> 00:18:47.890
You're nothing but a filthy traitor.

333
00:18:50.380 --> 00:18:54.120
If my life's going to hell,
I'm taking you with me.

334
00:18:56.850 --> 00:18:59.720
That is so cool!

335
00:18:57.250 --> 00:18:59.560
<b>The Sunny's Anchorage, Grove 17</b>

336
00:19:00.900 --> 00:19:02.720
Heck yeah!

337
00:19:03.670 --> 00:19:06.240
Can I get a body like that, too?

338
00:19:14.080 --> 00:19:15.950
So, can you, like, transform and stuff?

339
00:19:15.950 --> 00:19:18.280
Shoot beams? Missiles? Laser eyes?

340
00:19:18.280 --> 00:19:20.180
Hurry! Show me! Show me!

341
00:19:20.180 --> 00:19:21.420
I carry the dreams of men

342
00:19:21.420 --> 00:19:23.750
on my massive, metal shoulders!

343
00:19:23.750 --> 00:19:26.860
I'm back and better than ever!

344
00:19:26.860 --> 00:19:30.590
I'm not just me...

345
00:19:30.590 --> 00:19:33.000
I'm armored me, baby!

346
00:19:34.260 --> 00:19:36.430
Robot! Robot!

347
00:19:36.430 --> 00:19:40.040
I know he's cool! But stop
before you have a heart attack!

348
00:19:42.610 --> 00:19:44.110
One thing's buggin' me, though.

349
00:19:44.110 --> 00:19:46.380
Those giant robo-hands
are great for bashing,

350
00:19:46.380 --> 00:19:48.540
but how're you supposed
to do detail work?

351
00:19:50.470 --> 00:19:51.910
Never doubt the master.

352
00:19:51.910 --> 00:19:54.430
Whoa! Dude!

353
00:19:54.430 --> 00:19:56.110
He's got a hand in his hand!

354
00:19:58.230 --> 00:19:59.480
Robin!

355
00:20:06.490 --> 00:20:09.790
Wow, he looks terrible.
Did he do that to himself?

356
00:20:10.950 --> 00:20:12.960
Heh. It's Franky. Don't ask.

357
00:20:14.200 --> 00:20:16.500
Whoa, this must
be the coating, huh?

358
00:20:16.500 --> 00:20:19.440
Wanna see somethin'
else cool? Press my nose.

359
00:20:19.440 --> 00:20:20.240
Your nose?

360
00:20:20.590 --> 00:20:23.520
Press and hold it,
for three seconds or...

361
00:20:24.510 --> 00:20:27.460
Apply pressure to the
nasal region, human.

362
00:20:27.460 --> 00:20:29.900
Holy crap, he's like a real robot!

363
00:20:29.900 --> 00:20:32.300
Excited...

364
00:20:32.300 --> 00:20:35.750
One. Two. Three.

365
00:20:35.750 --> 00:20:37.480
Whoa! He grew hair!

366
00:20:40.820 --> 00:20:42.290
Wait a sec. Can you style it?

367
00:20:44.230 --> 00:20:45.330
Ahh. Easy as pie!

368
00:20:48.120 --> 00:20:51.760
Hey! Look who it is! What's up?

369
00:20:51.760 --> 00:20:53.460
Yeah, I see you.

370
00:20:53.460 --> 00:20:56.170
Ugh. Like our crew didn't
stick out enough already.

371
00:20:56.170 --> 00:20:58.900
Can I see your new
weapons, please? Can I?

372
00:21:02.910 --> 00:21:07.170
Sorry, buddy, that's the main event,
so we gotta wait till the captain shows up.

373
00:21:07.170 --> 00:21:07.970
Mecha.

374
00:21:07.970 --> 00:21:09.340
He made robot noises!

375
00:21:09.340 --> 00:21:11.170
Is "mecha" his new catchphrase?

376
00:21:13.980 --> 00:21:15.800
Hello there!

377
00:21:15.800 --> 00:21:18.100
Hey, Rayleigh! Hey, Shakky!

378
00:21:18.100 --> 00:21:21.710
Sorry to interrupt your reunion,
but we've kinda got an incident.

379
00:21:21.710 --> 00:21:24.470
Actually, two very large incidents
that demand your attention.

380
00:21:25.070 --> 00:21:26.740
Put the guitar down now!

381
00:21:27.260 --> 00:21:31.170
Hands in the air, pirate!
There's no escape!

382
00:21:32.410 --> 00:21:33.440
Members of the band...

383
00:21:34.730 --> 00:21:36.730
My lovely chorus...

384
00:21:36.730 --> 00:21:39.070
This will be my final song.

385
00:21:39.070 --> 00:21:41.240
Will you share it with me?

386
00:21:44.480 --> 00:21:46.190
Have no fear.

387
00:21:46.190 --> 00:21:50.030
My music has more than just
soul, it has true power.

388
00:21:50.030 --> 00:21:51.440
Are you insane?

389
00:21:51.830 --> 00:21:54.030
You think anyone's gonna
let you play another song?

390
00:21:54.370 --> 00:21:58.980
You might not see it this way, but I'm
grateful for the time we spent together.

391
00:21:58.980 --> 00:22:02.580
Thank you for these past two years,
and thank you for bringing me here.

392
00:22:02.580 --> 00:22:05.980
My crew and I have rather
tragic memories of this place.

393
00:22:07.150 --> 00:22:12.320
We lost an important battle here last
time, but we're ready to start anew.

394
00:22:12.320 --> 00:22:14.080
I'm the musician of the crew.

395
00:22:14.080 --> 00:22:16.180
I may possess some strength
as a swordsman,

396
00:22:16.180 --> 00:22:19.990
but my job is to make
our journey more fun.

397
00:22:19.990 --> 00:22:21.900
I've heard the stories.

398
00:22:21.900 --> 00:22:25.970
They think people are foolish enough
to believe that Straw Hat is dead.

399
00:22:25.970 --> 00:22:28.470
Well, you listen to me. He's not.

400
00:22:28.470 --> 00:22:31.480
Straw Hat Luffy is out there,
alive and kickin'!

401
00:22:31.480 --> 00:22:33.610
You can tell the world!

402
00:22:37.880 --> 00:22:39.780
And while you're at it,
tell them he's going to be

403
00:22:39.780 --> 00:22:42.050
the King of the Pirates someday, too!

404
00:22:42.050 --> 00:22:43.850
Boy, have I got some news for you guys.

405
00:22:43.850 --> 00:22:45.550
We better print this one in a jiffy!

406
00:22:45.550 --> 00:22:47.710
Yeah, baby, he's comin' back soon,

407
00:22:47.710 --> 00:22:51.420
and when he sets sail, I wanna
send him off Soul King style!

408
00:22:53.080 --> 00:22:54.520
That's so cool!

409
00:22:54.520 --> 00:22:56.960
Do you love me down to my bones?

410
00:22:56.960 --> 00:23:00.290
– Yeah!
– Yeah!

411
00:23:00.290 --> 00:23:02.360
I'll dedicate this to my crew.

412
00:23:02.360 --> 00:23:03.800
To my friends.

413
00:23:03.800 --> 00:23:08.830
My soul will sing to you
one last time! Yeah!

414
00:23:08.830 --> 00:23:12.380
Luffy, let's go to
the New World. Together.

415
00:23:12.380 --> 00:23:16.450
The show is over! I said you're
under arres... Would you shut up?!

416
00:23:18.420 --> 00:23:20.780
It's his last song! Let us hear it!

417
00:23:20.780 --> 00:23:22.450
Please, what harm could it do?

418
00:23:22.450 --> 00:23:23.520
She's right!

419
00:23:23.520 --> 00:23:26.420
You can wait till the show
is over, you bastards!

420
00:23:26.420 --> 00:23:29.760
Music is power.
Music is always on your side.

421
00:23:32.260 --> 00:23:33.900
One, two, three, four.

422
00:23:35.330 --> 00:23:37.030
I call this one "New World"!

423
00:23:42.870 --> 00:23:47.040
<b>Grove 46, Sabaody Archipelago</b>

424
00:23:44.670 --> 00:23:47.040
This is Grove #46 with an update.

425
00:23:47.140 --> 00:23:51.550
<b>Straw Hat Rendezvous Point</b>

426
00:23:47.530 --> 00:23:49.030
The pirates keep pouring in.

427
00:23:49.030 --> 00:23:51.200
There's definitely over a hundred now.

428
00:23:54.200 --> 00:23:55.800
None of the main Straw
Hats are here yet,

429
00:23:55.800 --> 00:23:59.730
but even so, I would approach
with extreme caution.

430
00:24:03.190 --> 00:24:05.330
Hey! What's wrong? Did they find you?

431
00:24:08.000 --> 00:24:10.200
This is bad! Tell the
backup they need to hurry!

432
00:24:10.650 --> 00:24:13.420
Well now, what have we here?

433
00:24:14.580 --> 00:24:17.080
Who is this little fellow
whispering behind the rock?

434
00:24:17.080 --> 00:24:19.750
Because he looks like a Navy soldier.

435
00:24:19.750 --> 00:24:22.050
And my goodness, what is this?

436
00:24:22.050 --> 00:24:25.860
You weren't looking to crash
our harmless party, were you?

437
00:24:29.890 --> 00:24:35.410
No! No! That's not very civil at all!

438
00:24:35.410 --> 00:24:37.870
'Cause if you were calling
your friends for backup,

439
00:24:37.870 --> 00:24:42.040
that would not end well,
seeing as they weren't invited.

440
00:24:42.040 --> 00:24:43.880
Show some manners.

441
00:24:43.880 --> 00:24:46.380
I saw him. He was calling.

442
00:24:46.380 --> 00:24:50.850
No! I was going to call them, but I...
I-I hadn't gotten through to them just yet.

443
00:24:50.850 --> 00:24:52.420
That is good to hear.

444
00:24:52.420 --> 00:24:54.190
And I say that for your sake, too.

445
00:24:55.190 --> 00:24:56.990
Because if your friends did show up,

446
00:24:57.320 --> 00:24:59.720
this grove would be covered in blood.

447
00:24:59.720 --> 00:25:03.690
Their blood and your blood.

448
00:25:03.690 --> 00:25:06.290
C'mon, Coribou. Back me up here.

449
00:25:06.290 --> 00:25:09.730
Huh? I wasn't listening!
I'm sorry! I'm sorry! I'm sorry!

450
00:25:09.730 --> 00:25:13.330
Who do you think you're bowing
to, moron? I'm over here!

451
00:25:14.490 --> 00:25:16.070
Please, forgive me.

452
00:25:16.070 --> 00:25:18.180
You still can't get it right!

453
00:25:18.180 --> 00:25:20.680
What, are you blind or just stupid?

454
00:25:20.680 --> 00:25:23.110
He's famous for killing Marines.

455
00:25:48.500 --> 00:25:52.030
Aww. Do you think this is a joke?

456
00:25:52.030 --> 00:25:53.590
He really stabbed that guy!

457
00:25:53.590 --> 00:25:55.600
Then the stories are true.

458
00:25:57.200 --> 00:25:59.370
Gods, have mercy!

459
00:25:59.370 --> 00:26:03.800
He is but a fool! He grabbed his gun!

460
00:26:03.800 --> 00:26:08.520
This poor, misguided soul tried
to incite violence against me!

461
00:26:08.520 --> 00:26:12.090
In your infinite kindness,
please show him mercy!

462
00:26:12.090 --> 00:26:16.150
Sorry, gods.
Sorry. Very sorry. Sorry, gods.

463
00:26:16.150 --> 00:26:18.270
Now, brother, bury him.

464
00:26:18.270 --> 00:26:20.870
Bury this sinful transgressor alive.

465
00:26:20.870 --> 00:26:23.570
Dig so that his poor soul may be free.

466
00:26:23.570 --> 00:26:24.360
Roger!

467
00:26:24.360 --> 00:26:25.720
Digging. Digging...

468
00:26:25.720 --> 00:26:27.190
Wait a second.

469
00:26:27.190 --> 00:26:30.120
What if I call them and
tell them not to come?

470
00:26:30.120 --> 00:26:32.060
That would be good, right?

471
00:26:32.060 --> 00:26:34.530
That's enough, Caribou.

472
00:26:34.870 --> 00:26:36.150
Huh?

473
00:26:36.460 --> 00:26:39.080
You can bury that nobody later.

474
00:26:39.080 --> 00:26:41.550
We got bigger fish to fry right now.

475
00:26:42.950 --> 00:26:45.220
Just tell us what you want
from us, Captain Luffy!

476
00:26:45.220 --> 00:26:46.620
We're ready to go!

477
00:26:48.250 --> 00:26:52.120
Take a look around you, boys,
this is history in the making!

478
00:26:52.120 --> 00:26:56.510
You probably don't know each other yet,
but you'll be tight as brothers soon enough.

479
00:26:56.510 --> 00:26:59.380
From here on out, you're Straw Hats!

480
00:27:02.450 --> 00:27:03.720
Not a bad deal.

481
00:27:03.720 --> 00:27:06.030
And I swear, when I become
King of the Pirates,

482
00:27:06.030 --> 00:27:08.270
you're gonna know you
made the right call!

483
00:27:08.270 --> 00:27:10.530
But I need a promise from ya first.

484
00:27:12.140 --> 00:27:15.980
'Cause a real king needs loyal subjects,
ones that will live and die for him

485
00:27:15.980 --> 00:27:17.650
and wait on him hand and foot!

486
00:27:19.350 --> 00:27:20.850
Anything you say!

487
00:27:20.850 --> 00:27:25.750
You're the man who escaped Impel Down,
wrecked Enies Lobby, stormed Marineford,

488
00:27:25.750 --> 00:27:27.590
and fought the Admirals!

489
00:27:27.590 --> 00:27:30.120
You've got the World Government
quaking in its boots!

490
00:27:30.120 --> 00:27:33.430
Sailing the seas with you
is like a dream come true!

491
00:27:33.430 --> 00:27:36.280
Listen, there's only one man
fit to be King of the Pirates

492
00:27:36.280 --> 00:27:37.940
and he's standing right there!

493
00:27:37.940 --> 00:27:40.310
You get with him, or you
get left in the dust!

494
00:27:44.120 --> 00:27:46.710
Looks like the gang's all here.

495
00:27:46.710 --> 00:27:48.440
Is this it?

496
00:27:48.440 --> 00:27:51.040
So where is everyone?
Stop makin' me wait!

497
00:27:55.810 --> 00:28:00.010
All right, enough!

498
00:28:00.010 --> 00:28:03.810
I didn't call you here to party,
we got business to attend to.

499
00:28:03.810 --> 00:28:07.980
Some jackasses out there haven't been
showin' me the respect I deserve.

500
00:28:07.980 --> 00:28:10.810
That is to say, they insulted my honor!

501
00:28:13.890 --> 00:28:17.220
A red-haired girl, a long-nosed
guy, and a brat with a backpack.

502
00:28:17.220 --> 00:28:18.990
Find 'em and bring 'em to me!

503
00:28:18.990 --> 00:28:21.640
The bastards are still on
the archipelago somewhere!

504
00:28:22.800 --> 00:28:24.640
Consider it done, boss!

505
00:28:24.640 --> 00:28:26.910
We'll make 'em suffer! You'll see!

506
00:28:29.020 --> 00:28:31.960
I gotta say, though, people sure
can change a lot in two years.

507
00:28:32.790 --> 00:28:34.730
For one, you guys hardly
talk at all anymore.

508
00:28:35.570 --> 00:28:37.140
He's more dangerous than we thought.

509
00:28:37.140 --> 00:28:40.930
We gotta get him to the boss pronto,
or he's gonna rat us out to everyone.

510
00:28:40.930 --> 00:28:42.230
Who is this guy?

511
00:28:42.230 --> 00:28:46.300
I dunno, but in the meantime, let's
try not to talk so he doesn't catch on.

512
00:28:46.300 --> 00:28:49.740
The captain's right there, he
can figure this out on his own!

513
00:28:49.740 --> 00:28:50.770
Sounds like a plan.

514
00:28:50.770 --> 00:28:54.480
I dunno what happened, but it seems like
you're gettin' along a lot better, too.

515
00:28:55.680 --> 00:28:57.520
Yep. Time changes lots of stuff.

516
00:28:59.450 --> 00:29:01.050
Like your faces, I mean.

517
00:29:01.050 --> 00:29:03.490
Unless you're wearing
a disguise like me.

518
00:29:11.440 --> 00:29:12.470
The Navy?

519
00:29:12.470 --> 00:29:13.780
That's right.

520
00:29:13.780 --> 00:29:18.110
They thought those Fake Straw Hats were
the real deal and mobilized their forces.

521
00:29:18.110 --> 00:29:19.810
Pacifistas, too.

522
00:29:19.810 --> 00:29:22.910
I have them wiretapped,
so there's no mistaking it.

523
00:29:22.910 --> 00:29:26.560
Anyway, Brook is finishing up his concert,
but I gave him a call backstage

524
00:29:26.560 --> 00:29:28.120
to let him know what was going on.

525
00:29:28.120 --> 00:29:30.960
He said he'd come after the
encore, so it shouldn't be long.

526
00:29:30.960 --> 00:29:34.460
Oh, yeah? Givin' up stardom
to be a lowly pirate?

527
00:29:34.460 --> 00:29:36.900
Goes without sayin',
but the man's got a backbone.

528
00:29:36.900 --> 00:29:39.030
All right, Nami, since
you're the navigator,

529
00:29:39.700 --> 00:29:43.580
there are a few tricks to operating
a coated ship I should pass on to you.

530
00:29:43.580 --> 00:29:44.300
Uh. Okay. Sure, let's hear it!

531
00:29:46.630 --> 00:29:48.540
We aren't getting ready
to take off, are we?

532
00:29:48.540 --> 00:29:50.340
We're still missing half the crew here!

533
00:29:50.340 --> 00:29:53.710
I mean, did Luffy even make
it to the archipelago yet?

534
00:29:53.710 --> 00:29:55.550
It's all under control!

535
00:29:55.550 --> 00:29:56.910
Captain!

536
00:29:56.910 --> 00:30:00.350
Huh? I'm kind of in the middle
of something, you goons!

537
00:30:00.350 --> 00:30:02.790
But we found the backpack
guy you was lookin' for.

538
00:30:02.790 --> 00:30:03.790
That's good, right?

539
00:30:03.790 --> 00:30:06.120
He's a "friend of the
crew," if you follow.

540
00:30:06.120 --> 00:30:07.290
Say hi.

541
00:30:10.790 --> 00:30:14.060
In other words, Luffy
arrived earlier this morning.

542
00:30:18.250 --> 00:30:19.750
It's almost time to go!

543
00:30:19.750 --> 00:30:22.520
I gave Sanji a baby Transponder
Snail when he stopped by,

544
00:30:22.520 --> 00:30:23.800
so I'll tell him to come back.

545
00:30:23.800 --> 00:30:25.500
He should have Zoro with him, too.

546
00:30:25.500 --> 00:30:26.470
Good.

547
00:30:26.470 --> 00:30:28.970
We should hurry,
because any moment now,

548
00:30:28.970 --> 00:30:32.040
the Navy will be attacking
with a sizable force.

549
00:30:32.040 --> 00:30:36.170
Unfortunately, there's no way
to contact your captain.

550
00:30:36.170 --> 00:30:39.510
But if you follow this Vivre card,
you should be able to hunt him down.

551
00:30:39.510 --> 00:30:41.860
Let's hope the fake Straw
Hats buy you a bit of time.

552
00:30:41.860 --> 00:30:45.390
Grove 42 is on the outskirts,
so it's close to the sea.

553
00:30:45.390 --> 00:30:48.900
Take the Sunny there and be ready
to depart on a moment's notice.

554
00:30:48.900 --> 00:30:51.670
I'm sure you'd like to relax
after these two difficult years,

555
00:30:51.670 --> 00:30:54.170
but it wasn't meant to be.

556
00:30:54.170 --> 00:30:57.410
The winds of the New
World wait for no one.
